From 6f6c1ff97d9f3758a811f069da0041ff59889b04 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emdee52 <emdee7101@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 13:31:39 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] port(MB-3): merge only the selected parts of one object into
 one part

New action on a multi-part selection: "Merge selected parts" unions exactly the
selected parts and replaces them in place, so the object, its instances, its
settings and every part that was not selected stay. The whole-object Mesh
boolean is untouched.

- libslic3r/OrcaExt/MergeParts: merge_parts_into_one() unions the selected
  MODEL_PART volumes in object space with the mcut pipeline the whole-object
  boolean uses; on refusal it joins them unwelded and reports it instead of
  losing them. The merged part takes the lowest selected index, its name and
  its per-part settings.
- GUI: boolean() takes a partial branch when two or more part rows are
  selected; can_mesh_boolean() also accepts that selection (same object, model
  parts only, no cut object, no text/SVG part); the multi-selection menu offers
  the item.
- MCP: boolean_parts gained the optional part_ids for the same path, and the
  handler sets the list's part selection mode first (selecting part rows in
  instance mode pops a modal "Selection conflicts" dialog that never returns).
- Tests: tests/libslic3r/test_model.cpp covers the object and untouched parts
  surviving, the parts' transforms being applied, a shared whole face welding,
  disjoint parts, and the refusals.

libslic3r suite 1728/1728; runtime check over MCP on a 3-part cut object
(3 -> 2 parts, object id kept, slice idle).
